esp-thread-lib-decompiled
========================================

This repository contains derivative work of esp-thread-lib by
Espressif (https://github.com/espressif/esp-thread-lib), licensed under
Apache License 2.0.

Changes from the original
-------------------------

- The original binary archive(s) matching esp32c3/*.a (static archives of
  compiled object files copyright Espressif) are decompiled into
  per-function C-like text files under decompiled/ using Ghidra
  (https://ghidra-sre.org/), an open-source software-reverse-engineering suite
  developed by the United States National Security Agency and released under
  Apache License 2.0.
- Each .o member of an archive is extracted with `ar x` and decompiled
  separately; each function within a member becomes its own .c file.
- Each .c file carries a header naming the upstream commit where that
  function's decompiled body last actually changed, plus provenance and
  license information.
- Commit history in this repository mirrors upstream commits that modified the
  target binary (one commit here per such upstream commit).

The decompiled output is mechanical and may be incomplete, structurally
different from the original source, or semantically inaccurate. It is not a
substitute for the original source code (which Espressif does not
publish for this library) and should not be treated as authoritative.

